/P 852 0 R
/E (The dataset comprised a total of 1,000 users. Initially, data from 25 individuals was validated at an ENT clinic to ensure accuracy by comparing results from traditional audiometry tests with those from the proposed App-Based Audiometer \(ABA\) tests. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 853 0 R
/E (Upon successful validation, the remaining data was collected from diverse locations to ensure wide demographic representation. The distribution of participants was as follows: gardens \(20%\), colleges \(10%\), residential societies \(20%\), hospitals \(8%\), public awareness campaigns \(32%\), and other sources \(10%\).)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 854 0 R
/E (Each data entry included parameters such as age, gender, and detailed hearing test results. The hearing tests measured the minimum intensity at which users could perceive tones at different frequencies. The frequencies tested were 250 Hz, 500 Hz, 1000 Hz, 2000 Hz, 4000 Hz, and 8000 Hz, with intensity levels ranging from 10 dB to 80 dB, in 10 dB increments.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
